-14j[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-14j/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reduce bead event streams into an actor-keyed touch index in [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-index[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-index: add the actor/bead touch reduction over [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]beads/events/streams, its versioned index wire, incremental [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]signature-cached refresh, and the read-only touch query, exposed through[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PyO3 bindings with fixture and parity tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt the touch index in Python and keep it fresh off the hot [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]path[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]host-refresh[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-index[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]host-refresh: add the Python facade over the new bindings, normalize [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]actors onto agent identities, and refresh the index incrementally from [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead mutation commits, post-sync refresh, and a bounded lumberjack [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]routine, with a doctor check.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase bead touched[/bold #D7AFFF]                                             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]bead-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after host-refresh[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead-cli: add the agent-scoped touch listing subcommand with colored and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]JSON output, and wire its help, ordering, and option contract to the CLI[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rules.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Resolve per-agent bead touches for the metadata panel[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-data[dim] · [dim][/dim]after host-refresh[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-data: add the mtime-cached per-agent touch loader, the summary [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]field and artifacts-lane resolution that carries it, and the merge that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]folds audited bead reads and the agent's own assigned beads into one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ranked per-bead view.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Render the Beads sub-section[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-render[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-data[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-render: paint the per-bead rows, verb chips, glyph and palette, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lane counts, hints, and clan aggregation, stop double-listing bead refs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]under Reads, and cover the result with header and visual tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Record agent bead views so unaudited reads are not silently [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]missing[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]bead-views[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-render[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead-views: record agent-attributed sase bead show invocations as a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]local viewed touch, merge them into the query behind the durable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mutation and audited-read facts, and render them as a visibly weaker [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]signal.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-14j","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-14j.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-a2fc7fc631acae951524e6e0fbab46b2","started_at":"202